# DRAFT (Story 10.2; Story 10.3 added Mid/Late): written from narrative-design.md's briefs and his voice rules. Raphael to rewrite.
# Den Fa, by the fire. first_contact plays once a run (it marks itself seen on its first line). Then his
# state (GameManager.den_fa_state, read as bridge.den_fa_state; it moves forward with the guild's
# reputation tier: Early, Mid at Known, Late at Trusted) picks: that state's entry title once (mid_enter,
# late_enter: each marks itself seen on its first line), then one of its numbered openings (early_N, mid_N,
# late_N), never the same one twice in a row (add mid_4 … and he uses it, no code change). Early asks and
# notices; Mid acknowledges, and knows what the guild has been through; Late is certain: he states, he
# doesn't ask. Game state comes only through `bridge` (scripts/dialogue/dialogue_bridge.gd).

~ first_contact
do bridge.mark_seen("den_fa_first_contact")
Den Fa: You keep looking at it. Most people stop, after a while.
- It's hard not to.
	Den Fa: No. It isn't.
- Looking at what?
	Den Fa: The pillar. You knew which.
- (Say nothing.)
	Den Fa: That's an answer too.
Den Fa: Sit, if you like. The fire has room for two.
if bridge.deaths_this_run > 0
	Den Fa: You've lost someone already. The fire is a good place not to talk about it.
=> END

~ early_1
Den Fa: Old stone remembers. Better than we do.
if bridge.reputation_tier_index >= 1
	Den Fa: They've started saying your guild's name at the bar. Not loudly. Yet.
=> END

~ early_2
Den Fa: Another day, and the sand still runs.
- Does it ever stop?
	Den Fa: Everything stops. That isn't the interesting part.
- I hadn't noticed.
	Den Fa: You had.
=> END

~ early_3
Den Fa: You're still here. Good.
if bridge.day >= 5
	Den Fa: {{bridge.day}} days. Most guilds don't last the first week.
=> END

~ mid_enter
do bridge.mark_seen("den_fa_mid_enter")
Den Fa: They speak of your guild at the bar now. I listen. You'd be surprised what people say near a fire.
if bridge.deaths_this_run > 0
	Den Fa: They speak of the ones who didn't come back, too. That's how a name is made. Partly.
Den Fa: Sit. You've earned a little of the warmth.
=> END

~ mid_1
Den Fa: {{bridge.adventurers_hired}} hired, this run. You choose them carefully. Or you think you do.
- I try.
	Den Fa: Trying is most of it. Not all.
- What's that supposed to mean?
	Den Fa: Exactly what it sounds like.
=> END

~ mid_2
Den Fa: The pillar's glow changed when you came in. Don't look. It does that.
=> END

~ mid_3
Den Fa: "{{bridge.reputation_tier}}," they call your guild now. A small word. It weighs more than it sounds.
if bridge.deaths_this_run > 0
	Den Fa: You paid for some of it. You know that already.
=> END

~ late_enter
do bridge.mark_seen("den_fa_late_enter")
Den Fa: You've stopped asking what the pillar is. Good. The question was never the right one.
Den Fa: The guild will outlast you. That isn't a threat. It's the point.
=> END

~ late_1
Den Fa: The sand runs the same for everyone. You've simply started to hear it.
- I don't hear anything.
	Den Fa: You will.
- How long have you been here?
	Den Fa: Long enough to know you'll ask that again.
=> END

~ late_2
Den Fa: Day {{bridge.day}}. You're further along than most. Further than you think.
=> END

~ late_3
Den Fa: You came in, you looked at the pillar, you sat down. Same as the first night. Not the same person.
=> END
